<title>SRI LANKA: S.Lanka May 97 M2 up 8.3 pct to 262.2 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>S.Lanka May 97 M2 up 8.3 pct to 262.2 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's broad money supply, or M2, grew by 8.3 percent year-on-year in May to 262.2 billion rupees, up from 242.1 billion a year ago, the Central Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank's weekly report said Sri Lanka's narrow money, or M1, representing mainly notes and coins in circulation, rose 4.7 percent year-on-year to 80.2 billion rupees, from 76.6 billion in May 1996.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
